{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 4800,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "10,000 years ago, the average human life lasted just over 30 years, and then a hundred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10480,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years ago that number was up to 50, and if you were born in the last few decades"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15940,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the developed world then your life expectancy is 80 years. But that is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of course assuming that no major breakthroughs happen during your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24240,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lifetime that can slow the process of aging, and that may be a very bad"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28880,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "assumption. There's a new series on National Geographic Channel which was developed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with GE and the show's creators wanted to present my take on aging, so I'm here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the GE Global Research Centre to talk to principal scientist Dr Fiona Ginty."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44780,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—...and this would be kind of an example of, you know, one of the types of images"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49280,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we would generate. So... —What are we looking at here? —So these are our cells that are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53640,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actively dividing, and these are cells are heading on their way to death"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58960,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or apoptosis. —Aging is not recognized as the disease. I mean, there are plenty of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64600,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "diseases we do acknowledge like diabetes, heart disease, Alzheimer's, and at their core"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70640,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aging may be responsible for all of them. And yet aging seems natural because it's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75960,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something that we do from birth and for a while it makes us better. Bigger,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80580,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stronger, faster, more intelligent. But then at some point in your life"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84960,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it reverses and aging makes our bodies decay and degrade. And why is that? Why do"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91880,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have to age? Why do our bodies have to decay? Well scientists are now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 97140,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "realizing there is a fundamental cellular mechanism at the heart of aging."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101780,
    "dDurationMs": 6100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do we age at the macroscopic level because our cells are aging at the microscopic level?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107880,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—To a great extent, yes. There's only a finite number of times a cell will divide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—A key discovery was made by a biologist named Hayflick. He was studying normal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119000,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "human cells and what he found was that they can only divide a finite number of times. On"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125080,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "average, it's about 50. Beyond that, the cell becomes senescent, which means it's an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131640,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aged cell. It can divide no longer. It lives for a little while but it's the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137120,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "accumulation of these senescent cells in our bodies that leads to aging on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142440,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "macroscopic scale. So it's as though cells have this little timer inside them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147080,
    "dDurationMs": 7720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that tells them when to stop dividing. But how do they know, and what is that timer?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154800,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—So telomeres are like how your shoelaces have, you know, a little bit of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160660,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plastic at the end to stop them from fraying. So telomeres are like the ends of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165480,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "your shoelaces —But for chromosomes? —But for chromosomes. So"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168460,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they keep the chromosome together and they stop it sticking to other chromosomes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173160,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So every time a cell divides, it loses some of the telomere. They estimate about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179200,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "200 base pairs. —Why is that? Why can't it just copy to the end? —You know, it's just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183840,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sort of really the mechanics of it. You know, there's only so much space when"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187400,
    "dDurationMs": 4100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "DNA polymerase does its job of replicating. —When it's copying? —Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191500,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—So the telomere getting shorter is like your molecular clock. The cellular clock"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197120,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside each cell that tells it how many times it has divided."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201680,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Would you want to have your telomeres measured? —Well, people do get their"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206280,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "telomeres measured. There have been associations made with lifestyle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210520,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with exercise, showing that longer telomeres are associated with a more active"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215780,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lifestyle, exercise. —What if there was a way to stop the telomeres from"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220460,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shortening? If we could do that, maybe the cells would live forever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 225900,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—There's another enzyme involved called telomerase, and it keeps rebuilding. Like,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230400,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it doesn't let the telomere ever shrink, so it... —It rebuilds the telomere? —Right, exactly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235920,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "—There is one animal that doesn't seem to age, and that is the lobster. It just gets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242800,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bigger over time. It doesn't get weaker and its chromosomes don't change. It has"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246780,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long telomeres that do not shorten, so it only dies when it gets eaten by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252400,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "something else, like us. So how can we be more like a lobster? Some people would"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259760,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say maybe I want my telomerase to be higher for longer. Would that help? I mean,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265720,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would that keep us younger? —I mean it's balance, because, you know, in cancer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269660,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you've got a perfect example of telomerase being active and it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 273560,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "becomes an unregulated growth situation. —This is the double-edged sword of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279200,
    "dDurationMs": 8840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "telomeres and telomerase. Cancer cells have really long telomeres, and they can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288040,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divide indefinitely, and that is the problem with cancer. Cancer is dividing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293840,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cells that won't stop and they won't die. So, in a way, cancer is the immortal cell"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301440,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "living within us. So maybe we've developed the aging process. Maybe we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307240,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have telomeres that shorten for a very good reason – because otherwise they could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312720,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "become cancerous. —So one of the theories there is that the cells divide that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317360,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "limited number of times because it stops them from accumulating damage that may be detrimental."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324560,
    "dDurationMs": 5220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there is some... —It might cause them to become cancer. —Exactly. —Over the past hundred"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329780,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years, developments in medicine have increased human lifespan more than we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333500,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could have imagined, and I can only expect that the next hundred years will bring"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 338300,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "similarly incredible results. I'm not sure where or how they will take place,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343720,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you can bet that your life expectancy today will not be the actual age at which you die."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353620,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you want to find out more about the future of aging, well then you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "should definitely check out the episode of Breakthrough which was directed by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360280,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ron Howard. That's airing on Sunday, November 29 at 9/8c. That is just"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366380,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of six episodes of Breakthrough which was developed by National Geographic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369980,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Channel and GE. So I want to thank them for supporting Veritasium, and I want"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374200,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to thank you for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, and I also made a video about the future of energy. It's over on the GE"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381000,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "YouTube channel, so go check it out!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
